# mindone_fsd init service.
#
# NOTE (see README-INTEGRATION.md "ccci_fsd has no stock init service"):
# the stock init.cccifsd.rc on this device has ONLY mkdir/restorecon
# lines, no "service ccci_fsd ..." stanza at all -- disassembly of the
# stock ccci_mdinit binary shows it statically links the same file-service
# logic (function fsd_main(), thread names "ccci_fsd(0)"/"ccci_fsd(1)")
# and appears to run it as an internal pthread rather than exec'ing a
# separate process, even though a standalone /vendor/bin/ccci_fsd binary
# also exists on the partition (126 KB, unused by any service on this
# build as far as this recon found).
#
# mindone_fsd is deliberately kept as its OWN separate process (matching
# this task's four-daemon deliverable shape and ccci_fsd.te's existing,
# already-correct standalone sepolicy domain) rather than folded into
# mindone_mdinit as a thread. This is a documented, deliberate
# architectural deviation from the stock binary's internal shape -- NOT a
# functional gap, since the wire protocol on /dev/ccci_fs is identical
# either way and does not care which process serves it.

service ccci_fsd /vendor/bin/ccci_fsd
    user radio
    group radio system
    class core
    oneshot
